00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:01.790
Did you decide on what to get her?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.950
Did you think of something good?

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:08.130
W-Well, sort of...

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:11.090
Maybe a bike?

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.050
A bike?

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:19.380
A bike in return for 
obligatory chocolate?

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.170
Are you a millionaire?

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:23.880
I have other ideas, too.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:27.720
I was thinking about making her 
a meat and potatoes dish with

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:28.810
the potatoes I got from home.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.410
Rejected.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:33.540
Miss Sasako.

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:35.240
Yes?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:39.750
It's a little early, 
but it's almost White Day.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:40.740
Here's your present.

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.250
This is...

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.710
Um...

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:51.690
It's Göreme National Park and the
 Rock Sites of Cappadocia made out of candy.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:56.530
That's amazing and all, 
but it's hard to tell.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.010
It's a World Heritage Site.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.680
Thank you...

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:02.140
Bamboo Grass Fish Cakes

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:05.120
Here's mine, Miss Sasako.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:08.570
Don't ask me why they're 
bamboo grass fish cakes.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.610
Thank you very much...

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.610
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:31.140
It's finally White Day today,

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.960
but were you able to 
find her a present?

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:38.150
Er, well... y-yeah...

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:39.880
Uh...

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:44.260
You usually give them clothes, right?

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:45.590
Usually?

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.350
Or maybe bath towels?

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:55.930
Er, it's not something you 
can have too much of.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:58.150
Um, um...

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.070
Water? And why so much?

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:05.330
I didn't know what to do anymore!

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:07.510
Rejected.

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:08.040
Definitely.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:10.990
I think sweets like marshmallows

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:12.670
or candy would be just fine.

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:17.130
All right. I'll do that.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.090
Polar 
Bear 
Café

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:22.900
Thank you for all of your hard work.

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:25.490
Thank you!

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:36.320
Welcome!

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:40.740
Miss Sasako.

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.620
Miss Sasako?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.530
Oh, yes?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.770
The caffè latte is ready.

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.270
Are you okay?

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:52.530
Yes...

00:19:58.210 --> 00:19:59.640
Thank you for waiting.

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:04.220
By the way, Polar Bear...

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:04.930
Yes?

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.370
I have to wonder what Mr. Handa is doing.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:23.470
Huh?

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.470
Mr. Penguin,

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:30.160
I have left-over candy... 
would you like it?

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:36.760
I'm scared to see it, but sure.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.700
All right, here you go.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.500
The Sagrada Família...

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:45.840
Correct!

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:48.200
And in its finished form.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.810
Got it done a lot faster 
than the original.

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.960
You didn't have to make 
it out of candy.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:55.740
Um...

00:20:57.230 --> 00:21:00.190
I'm sorry, Mr. Polar Bear...

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:11.480
Mr. Handa?

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:15.540
Oh, Miss Sasako.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:18.890
What's wrong? Don't you have work?

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:21.970
I requested to leave early.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:23.970
Leave early?

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:27.240
I think I may have a fever.

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:29.470
Do you have a cold?

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.890
I don't usually catch them, but...

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:36.560
Oh, I know.

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:40.360
Here, take these.

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.780
Oh, thank you very much.

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:47.200
I hope you feel better soon.

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:50.730
Thank you very much.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:08.820
How was White Day?

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:11.060
What did you give her?

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.060
Mandarins!

00:22:13.530 --> 00:22:16.170
Mandarins?

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:19.000
Yeah, mandarins!

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.990
Next Time

00:23:58.060 --> 00:23:59.960
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:01.460
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:03.160
Do you know what qigong is?

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.260
I do.

00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:04.960
Ha!

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:10.220
Could you not do that?

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:11.730
May I try, too?

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:13.010
Ha!

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.100
Stop!

00:24:15.630 --> 00:24:16.660
Let's end this.

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:18.440
In next week's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:20.990
we'll be bringing you this 
week's Polar Bear's Café.

00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:21.610
Ha!

00:24:21.610 --> 00:24:23.800
I said stop!

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:24.000
Mr. Grizzly's Reunion
Mr. Llama's Time Capsule

00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:24.000
Enjoy!
